      "writtenOn": "2025-03-20T09:31:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "nit: this doesn\u0027t need to be specific to Vulkan. D3D12 also usses an allocator and maybe Metal in the future. WDYT of using `totalAllocatedMemory` and `totalUsedMemory` with an explanation about the fragmentation? `totalUsage` would be redundant I believe? Then in the frontend we could assume that `totalAllocatedMemory` can be set to `totalUsedMemory` by default and backends will override if needed.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 337,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 339,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "fcf16aaebbb9a2f365f9a6b453670d221e9b4c2e",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5aefab0c_aa1e33fa",
        "filename": "include/dawn/native/DawnNative.h",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 339,
      "author": {
        "id": 1004831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-20T13:49:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Maybe `allocatorTotalUsedMemory` vs `allocatorTotalAllocatedMemory` just to make it clear this is the allocators bookkeeping? Right now the two total used memory from adding up buffers+textures can be different than ResourceMemoryAllocators total used due to timing of when deallocations no longer count as used.\n\nI believe `totalUsage` isn\u0027t needed indepenent of this CL. It\u0027s used [here](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:gpu/command_buffer/service/dawn_context_provider.cc;l\u003d865;drc\u003d4c6d5b3c3ed16fa75258c6b4763188f840cb433d) to give a total for `gpu/dawn/device_X/`. I think the memory dump code will just add up all the sub-allocations aka `gpu/dawn/device_X/textures` + `gpu/dawn/device_X/buffers` which gives the same value. If so we can remove it and the code to create that dump. Even if not we don\u0027t need a separate struct member the Chrome code can `mem_usage.texturesUsage + mem_usage.buffersUsage`?",
      "parentUuid": "8a935203_9fc5c222",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 337,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 339,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "fcf16aaebbb9a2f365f9a6b453670d221e9b4c2e",
